# Qt's five dialogs as Chimera shows them: drawn inside the window that
# opens them. Qt 6.10 and later put the dialogs it draws itself (Linux's;
# Windows' are the system's own) in a window of their own, and on WSL a
# person found that window's Open and Cancel did nothing (issue 389), as
# others have found of Qt's child windows there. Chimera's QML imports
# ChimeraDialogs in place of QtQuick.Dialogs; everything else, the enums
# among it, comes from QtQuick.Dialogs. On Linux the file and folder dialogs
# are the desktop's own chooser, or Chimera's where there is none
# (PickerBase.qml); FileDialog keeps Qt's FileMode enum.
module ChimeraDialogs
import QtQuick.Dialogs auto
FileDialog 6.0 FileDialog.qml
FolderDialog 6.0 FolderDialog.qml
internal PickerBase PickerBase.qml
internal BuiltinChooser BuiltinChooser.qml
MessageDialog 6.0 MessageDialog.qml
ColorDialog 6.0 ColorDialog.qml
FontDialog 6.0 FontDialog.qml
